<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.relogin — hourly cadence for `cc-relogin-poll`: catch the T−7d login-renewal window
  and escalate at T−48h if no k==0 moment was ever caught.

  WHY launchd and not a Claude hook: a hook dies with its session and only ever runs while a
  session is alive. The login deadline does not care — it can fall on a weekend, mid-reboot, or
  any stretch with no session running at all. Only a launchd job ticks when nothing is alive,
  which is exactly the window this cadence exists to cover.

  WHY `export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:$PATH"` in the command: `zsh -lc` runs a LOGIN shell, which
  sources .zprofile/.zlogin but NOT .zshrc — where the ~/.claude/bin PATH entry lives. Without the
  explicit export, `cc-relogin-poll` (and the `cc-relogin` / `claude-accounts` it shells out to) is
  not on PATH and the job fails silently every hour. Previously observed; do not remove.

  RunAtLoad is FALSE deliberately: loading the job must not fire an immediate re-login attempt.
  The first tick comes one StartInterval (1h) later, on the normal schedule.

  WHY this file lives in launchd/staged/ and not launchd/: install.sh globs `launchd/*.plist` and
  bootstraps every match, so a staged plist in that directory is activated by anyone merely
  RUNNING THE INSTALLER. Copying-without-bootstrapping is not a safe middle ground either —
  launchd bootstraps everything in ~/Library/LaunchAgents at the next login, so the copy IS the
  activation. A plain glob cannot descend into a subdirectory, so this location is immune BY
  CONSTRUCTION. Do not move this file up a level, and do not make that glob recursive;
  tests/install-staged-plist.bats pins both halves.

  🚨 STAGED, NOT LOADED. This file ships inert — loading it is C10 OPERATOR ACTIVATION and is
  explicitly out of scope for the build that authored it. No agent may run launchctl on it.

  OPERATOR ACTIVATION (your call, when you want the cadence live):
      cp launchd/staged/com.claude.relogin.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.claude.relogin.plist
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.claude.relogin.plist
      launchctl list | grep com.claude.relogin          # verify it is registered
  Dry-run it first (invokes nothing, mutates nothing):
      cc-relogin-poll --dry-run --json
  Deactivate:
      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.claude.relogin
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>            <string>com.claude.relogin</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:$PATH"; cc-relogin-poll --once</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key>    <integer>3600</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>        <false/>
  <key>ProcessType</key>      <string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key>    <true/>
  <key>Nice</key>             <integer>10</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>  <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/cc-relogin-poll.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/cc-relogin-poll.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
